# 8. HERO OPENING ANIMATION

Build a coordinated GSAP timeline.

The animation should complete in approximately 3–3.5 seconds, but must remain interruptible.

Do not block the form while the intro plays.

## Phase A — Atmosphere

The background gently brightens.

Soft lavender, ice-blue, and peach illumination appears behind the workspace.

The wordmark and eyebrow become visible.

## Phase B — Typography

The headline reveals through elegant line masks.

The paragraph follows.

The form enters through subtle opacity and vertical movement.

Do not animate every character individually.

## Phase C — Glass assembly

The Input panel slides into position from a shallow depth.

The AI Processing panel enters from a slightly different spatial layer.

The Output panel settles into its corresponding location.

Use slight rotation, position, and scale interpolation.

The motion should have weight and polish.

No cartoon bouncing.

## Phase D — Workflow connection

SVG connectors draw themselves between the panels.

Small light signals begin moving along the connection paths.

These signals must follow the actual connector geometry.

## Phase E — Processing demonstration

Highlight an incoming task.

Animate it progressing into the AI Processing panel.

Sequentially highlight:

Classify → Summarize → Route.

The Output panel reveals the corresponding organized result.

This is an illustrative deterministic demonstration.

Do not claim a live AI model is processing information unless an actual inference system is connected.

## Phase F — Rest state

The workspace settles into quiet ambient motion.

The form remains clearly visible.

Do not endlessly replay the complete introduction.

